well now to our exclusive with Real  Housewife of New Jersey Teresa Giudice  interview since a judge ruled that her  husband Joe would be deported to Italy  after serving his three-year prison  sentence for bankruptcy fraud our Brooke  Anderson talked to Teresa about that  traumatizing moment what was the first  thing that went through your mind when  the judge issued that order of  deportation like I was I was devastated  we live in this country of freedom and  everything you're supposed to keep  families together not break them apart  did you ever think that could be a  possibility I mean very slim chance just  because you know it is a white-collar  crime Joe called to you after the  hearing did he cry no you know it takes  both of us a lot to cry when we spoke  with him last he did seem strong and and  tough you know I think going to jail is  easy part I just want to get out you  know as quickly as I can  but do you think that is an act is he  just trying to be that way no I said I  doesn't break down I'm sure he guys but  you know I mean I know this whole thing  is killing him inside and you know he  feels you know just guilty about  everything do you think the judge was  too harsh the judge went by the law and  you know so now we have the right to  appeal and that's where we're gonna go  Teresa tells me the hardest part of the  situation is watching the toll it has  taken on their four daughters aged 9 to  17 how did you tell them what's going on  my brother called gia because he heard  it on the news so that's how my oldest  found out and I was really upset I took  ivory Lynn Milania together  Gabriella teared up Milania hysterical  like she was like a mess your youngest  is only nine years old does she even  comprehend what's happening um she's the  only one that I didn't tell Joe has been  gone since she's six and it's sad like  she needs her daddy home how his prison  changed him he's definitely changed for  the better for the better  how's he doing he looks amazing I think  he looks the best he ever looked is he  working out a lot is he what's he doing  in there when I met him he weighed 160  and now he's 170 so he's pumping a  little iron he's hard as a rock  [Music]
 

